From 37fccd4262cf92368a8068431d9d779cbc4724e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mark Vis <118430440+mark-vis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 16:59:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/14] Add hook caption/prepare and socket caption/listentry

\@caption now executes the new hook caption/prepare
{type}{star}{list text}{text} after the \par, for every caption (also
for \caption* and for direct calls of \@caption), and writes the list
entry through the new socket caption/listentry {type}{list text}{text}
(not for \caption*). The default plug kernel writes the entry with
\addcontentsline as before, so the output does not change. At the time
of the hook \@currentlabel is set, and \@currentHref if the step made a
target; it is the place for code that today wraps \@caption (e.g., to
make its own target, with \@captiontargetfalse in caption/before and
\@kernel@caption@unique for a caption that does not step). The
settings for a replaced \@caption are undone before the hook, and a
number reserved for it is given back before it, so the hook and the
plug see the normal definitions.

caption/listentry has three arguments, the caption text too, so a plug
can use it when the list text was not given (it can record in
caption/before whether it was).

\@caption keeps its release block ("caption body"); it still typesets
with \@kernel@caption@typeset (the socket caption/typeset is added by
"Add socket caption/typeset and the kernel copy \@kernel@@caption").

New test caption-interface-006 (hook and plug arguments, \caption*,
direct calls, a wrapper of the kernel \@caption, a client that names
its own target in caption/prepare); caption-interface-002 checks that
the new hook is not executed after a roll-back. The hook-list .tlg
files list the new hook.
